e and you know that that that fight  that we had in us the summer of 2020  keep that same energy because we wrote  this song out of pain we wrote the song  out of hope we wrote this song thinking  that you know  um  we want things to change this song has  been a soundtrack to some people's March  when they were out there protesting the  lives of people that we've lost you know  um  it just it's I can't even I don't have  words for that feeling you know it means  so much to me and we still have a lot of  work to do prior to the show E.T caught  up with the recording Academy's interim  president who said inclusivity and  representation was top of mind I think  the Grammys are always trying to change  we're trying to evolve and since I've  been here for the short period that I  have which is a year I think we've made  huge strides and we'll continue to but  we want to be the most relevant and the  most respectful most inclusive  organization that really really  represents the craft and the Excellence  around music making so hopefully we'll  see more progress that's my goal and  after a little baby's performance he  told E.T it took a lot of work to pull  it off how did you all pull off the  little baby performance in multiple sets  everybody around different places it was  a lot of work actually it was  choreographed beat for beat for beat it  was just right outside the convention  center right there on on the street and  it was just a lot of work a lot of  planning a lot of rehearsing and uh to  nail it  foreign

